  "src": "Blind Deep-Stalker.md",
  "customTables": [
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Pack's Tactic (Encounter Setup & Combat Behavior)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Pack Behavior | Setup & Mechanical Execution |",
     "|:--|:--|:--|",
     "| **1** | **The Silence Ambush** | The blind deep-stalkers have been crouching in total darkness for hours, conserving all sound. They cannot be heard with passive Perception. The first sign of their presence is a club connecting with the rearmost PC. |",
     "| **2** | **The Sound Funnel** | The blind deep-stalkers have spent time filling a passage with debris that will crumble loudly when stepped on. Every step the party takes generates a locating sound the blind deep-stalkers triangulate without error. They know exactly where each PC is. The party does not know where the blind deep-stalkers are. |",
     "| **3** | **The Torch Hunters** | Light is a targeting beacon, not a comfort. Any PC carrying a light source in blind deep-stalker territory is giving every blind deep-stalker within 30 ft. a free Perception check to pinpoint their exact location. The blind deep-stalkers will close on the light-bearer first, specifically to eliminate the party's psychological comfort. |",
     "| **4** | **The Dung Trail** | The party has unknowingly walked through a blind deep-stalker scent marker — a smear of viscera on the floor that signals \"intruder.\" Every blind deep-stalker in the dungeon now knows which corridor they're in and roughly what they smell like. DC 15 Survival to recognize the marker before stepping on it. |",
     "| **5** | **The Illusion Immunity** | A spellcaster in the party tries a *minor illusion*, *silent image*, or *major image*. The blind deep-stalkers don't blink. They redirect toward the sound of the spellcaster's voice and footsteps, completely ignoring the illusion. |",
     "| **6** | **The Surface Raid** | The blind deep-stalkers have surfaced at night to abduct livestock or people from an isolated farmstead. They are unnerved by the open space and move in tighter formations than normal — but they can still track by scent across a dirt field better than any tracker the party has. |",
     "| **7** | **The Mind-Thief's Vanguard** | The blind deep-stalkers are escorting a mind-thief through the Deeplands toward a humanoid settlement. The flayer stays 30 ft. back and directs the blind deep-stalkers telepathically. Killing the blind deep-stalkers does not stop the flayer. The flayer is watching everything. |",
     "| **8** | **The Captive Caravan** | A chain of four abducted humanoids — hands bound, heads covered — is being herded through the tunnels by a group of blind deep-stalkers. The blind deep-stalkers respond to any liberation attempt by immediately scattering into the dark with their captives. |",
     "| **9** | **The Deafening Option** | A creative party might use a *thunderwave*, a bell, or an improvised loud noise to temporarily Deafen all blind deep-stalkers in range, reducing their Blindsight from 30 ft. to 10 ft. The blind deep-stalkers respond to this by immediately closing to melee range — they know what it means when they can't hear. |",
     "| **10** | **The Tracker's Nightmare** | The party killed a blind deep-stalker earlier and continued into the dungeon without concern. Blind Deep-Stalkers can smell the blood of their own dead from 60 ft. The entire local pack has been converging on the party's trail since that kill. They arrive at the end of this encounter as reinforcements — from behind. |"
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Blind Deep-Stalker Lair (Investigation & Signs of Occupation)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Environmental Sign | What It Means |",
     "|:--|:--|:--|",
     "| **1** | **The Smooth Wall Path** | A specific corridor has had all sharp edges and loose stones meticulously removed at shoulder height — a clearly navigated path made safe by touch over years of use. DC 12 Survival to recognize this as a cleared travel route. |",
     "| **2** | **The Scent Boundary** | A horizontal smear of viscera across the tunnel at chest height. DC 13 Survival: this is a territorial marker. Something on the other side of this line considers this its space. |",
     "| **3** | **The Sound Map** | Small pebbles have been wedged into specific cracks in the walls, each producing a subtly different tone when the air pressure changes. DC 15 Investigation to realize the entire cavern is instrumented as an acoustic early warning system. |",
     "| **4** | **The Bone Graffiti** | Bones from past kills have been wedged into wall crevices in a pattern — not decorative, but functional. DC 14 Arcana or DC 12 with Undercommon: these are navigation markers, telling blind deep-stalkers which tunnels lead to water, food, or their masters. |",
     "| **5** | **The Missing Stones** | Certain floor stones in the corridor are absent — removed and placed 5 ft. away. The gaps are barely visible in low light. Stepping in one: DC 12 Dex save or turn an ankle (Disadvantage on Dex checks for 1 hour). The blind deep-stalkers know exactly where each gap is. |",
     "| **6** | **The Stripped Campsite** | A previous party's campsite, stripped of everything edible or scented. The sleeping rolls remain. The food sacks, the tallow candles, and the party's rope (soaked in sweat) are gone. The blind deep-stalkers took everything they could smell. |",
     "| **7** | **The Fresh Blood** | A trail of human blood leads deeper into the dungeon. DC 12 Medicine: the blood is from multiple people, dripping at irregular intervals — consistent with a stumbling prisoner being herded. This is recent. Within the last two hours. |",
     "| **8** | **The Mind-Thief Shrine** | A crude altar of stacked stone bearing a carved tentacled face. Blind Deep-Stalkers leave fresh kills here — sometimes still moving — as offerings. The offerings are always gone by the next day. |",
     "| **9** | **The Echo Chamber** | A natural cavern in the territory has extraordinary acoustics — voices from the entrance can be heard anywhere in the cavern. The blind deep-stalkers use this as their meeting point. Any conversation the party has here is overheard by every blind deep-stalker within range. |",
     "| **10** | **The Survivor** | A captured adventurer, half-mad from days in absolute darkness, has managed to hide in a crevice the blind deep-stalkers can't reach. They have been surviving on dripping water. They know the layout of this section of the dungeon better than anyone alive — and they are desperate enough to tell the party everything if freed. |"
    ]
   }
  ],
