    "text": "**Cataclysmic Event (Recharge 4-6).** The cataclysm creates one of the following effects at random (roll 1d4):\n  - **1: Clinging Flames.** Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 23, each creature in a 60-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. Failure: 45 (13d6) Fire damage. Failure or Success: The target starts burning.\n  - **2: Freezing Waves.** Strength Saving Throw: DC 23, each creature in a 90-foot Cone. Failure: 22 (5d8) Bludgeoning damage plus 22 (5d8) Cold damage, and the target has the Prone condition. Success: Half damage only.\n  - **3: Raging Storm.** A storm cloud fills a 60-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. The cloud lasts for 1 minute or until the cataclysm uses Cataclysmic Event again. Creatures entirely in the cloud have the Blinded and Deafened conditions and can't cast spells with a Verbal component. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 23, each creature that enters the cloud for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there. Failure: 18 (4d8) Lightning damage plus 18 (4d8) Thunder damage. Success: Half damage.\n  - **4: Swallowed Earth.** Strength Saving Throw: DC 23, one creature of up to Huge size originating from a point on the ground the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. Failure: 18 (4d8) Acid damage plus 18 (4d8) Acid damage, and the target is buried under rubble in an unoccupied space. A buried target has the Restrained condition, has Total Cover, and is suffocating. As an action, a buried creature or another creature within 5 feet can make a DC 18 Strength (Athletics) check. On a successful check, the creature is no longer buried. Success: Half damage only.",
