  "customTables": [
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Ghast's Lair & Ecosystem (Tone Variance Table)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "|d10|Encounter Premise|Campaign Tone / Mechanics|",
     "|:--|:--|:--|",
     "|**1**|**The Gourmet Aristocrat**|**Humorous:** The ghast wears a decaying tuxedo, a bib, and speaks with a high-class accent. It refuses to eat the party's dwarf because \"the meat is too tough,\" instead demanding they fetch it a plump halfling in exchange for passage.|",
     "|**2**|**The Bureaucratic Warden**|**Lighthearted:** A Gravecaller has unionized the local undead. The party must fill out extensive paperwork in triplicate and pay a \"grave tax\" in silver to cross the cemetery, or face a highly organized, whistle-blowing strike force of ghouls.|",
     "|**3**|**The Siren's Trap**|**Pulp / Adventure:** A ghast is using an illusion or a captured, paralyzed bard to call for help from a deep pit. When the PCs throw down a rope, the ghast yanks the rope to pull the rescuer down into a swarm of waiting ghouls.|",
     "|**4**|**The Submerged Lacedons**|**Swashbuckling:** Aquatic ghasts (Lacedons) lurk beneath the docks. They paralyze sailors and immediately drag them into the water, using drowning as a secondary hazard while their paralyzation takes hold.|",
     "|**5**|**The Iron Ward**|**Tactical / Puzzle:** The PCs find a ruined temple protected by a circle of powdered cold iron. The ghasts are trapped outside, throwing rocks and trying to trick the PCs into breaking the iron line so the pack can swarm inside.|",
     "|**6**|**The Tactical Retreat**|**Gritty / Suspense:** The ghasts refuse to fight a fair battle. They strike from the shadows, paralyze one party member, and immediately drag the paralyzed victim into the dark, forcing the party into a frantic pursuit.|",
     "|**7**|**The Spellstitched Cult**|**Dark Fantasy:** The party encounters ghasts covered in glowing blue runes. They use _Darkness_ spells to extinguish all torches, fighting in complete magical pitch-black while utilizing their 60 ft. Darkvision.|",
     "|**8**|**The Sickened Survivors**|**Horror:** A village is under siege. The town guards are all retching and violently ill from the ghasts' overwhelming Stench, fighting with Disadvantage on all attacks. The PCs must hold the line while the guards recover.|",
     "|**9**|**The Elven Arrogance**|**Tragic / Investigation:** The party finds the half-eaten corpse of an elven champion. The elf's journal boasts of their racial immunity to ghoul paralysis, proving they fatally underestimated the abyssal power of a true Ghast.|",
     "|**10**|**The White Kingdom Envoy**|**Epic / High Fantasy:** The Gravecaller is an ambassador from Doresain, the Ghoul King. It offers the PCs a horrific alliance: the ghasts will aid them against a local dragon, provided the party allows the ghasts to eat the town's prisoners.|"
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Charnel Trail (Investigation & Clues)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "|d10|Discovery in the Dirt|Investigative Hook|",
     "|:--|:--|:--|",
     "|**1**|**The Sorted Pantry**|The PCs find a hidden cave where corpses aren't just tossed aside; they are meticulously hung from meat hooks and sorted by race and age, showing high-level, horrific intelligence.|",
     "|**2**|**The Rusted Iron**|A pile of discarded weapons. A DC 13 Investigation check reveals that only the cold-forged iron weapons have been deliberately snapped or thrown into a pool of acid to destroy them.|",
     "|**3**|**The Missing Heads**|Graves have been exhumed, but the skulls have been carefully removed to be carved into magical focuses (Spellstitched Runes) or used in the creation of Flameskulls.|",
     "|**4**|**The Perfumed Handkerchief**|Dropped near a grave, a handkerchief drenched in overpowering, cheap perfume. A local gravedigger has been using it to block out the Ghast's Stench aura while secretly working for them.|",
     "|**5**|**The Abyssal Scrawlings**|A crypt door is covered in Abyssal runes drawn in dried blood, translating to \"the Death-Lord Provides.\" It confirms the ghouls are being bolstered by fiendish magic.|",
     "|**6**|**The Trapped Tunnel**|A subterranean tunnel where the ceiling has been deliberately rigged to collapse. Mindless ghouls don't build traps, proving a cunning Ghast is coordinating the lair's defense.|",
     "|**7**|**The Untouched Silver**|A pristine silver holy symbol lying in a pile of filth. The ghasts refuse to touch it, suggesting a weakness or a lingering fear of the deity it represents.|",
     "|**8**|**The Stitched Skin**|A scrap of leathery skin bearing intricate, magical sutures. An Arcana check (DC 14) reveals someone is actively crafting Spellstitched undead in the region.|",
     "|**9**|**The Counterfeit Guard**|A freshly paralyzed local guardsman is found bound and gagged in a crypt, while his uniform is missing. A ghast is using the armor to disguise itself in the foggy city streets.|",
     "|**10**|**The Desecrated Earth**|A massive, 30-foot circle of spongy, black earth that radiates cold. A Gravecaller has permanently cast an aura of _Desecration_ here, buffing all undead that fight within its borders.|"
    ]
   }
  ],
