  "actions": [
   {
    "text": "**Strength Drain:** _Melee Weapon Attack:_ +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. _Hit:_ 9 (2d6 + 2) necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4. The target dies if this reduces its Strength to 0. Otherwise, the reduction lasts until the target finishes a short or long rest. If a non-evil humanoid dies from this attack, a new shadow rises from the corpse in 1d4 hours.\n\n---",
    "name": "Strength Drain",
    "atk": 4,
    "reach": 5,
    "dmg": [
     {
      "n": 2,
      "die": 6,
      "bonus": 2,
      "type": "necrotic"
     }
    ],
    "kind": "melee"
   }
  ],
  "bonus": [],
  "reactions": [],
  "legendary": [],
  "role": "lurker",
  "habitat": [
   "ruins",
   "cave",
   "deeplands",
   "urban"
  ],
  "treasure": "none",
  "activity": [
   "night"
  ],
  "factionFit": [
   "undead-court"
  ],
  "src": "Shadow.md",
  "customTables": [
   {
    "heading": "d10 Shadow Encounters (Tone Variance Table)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Encounter Premise | Campaign Tone / Mechanics |",
     "|:----|:------------------|:--------------------------|",
     "| **1** | **The Darkening Room** | **Horror Buildup:** As the party explores, torches begin going out one by one — not from wind, but drained. The shadows are feeding on the light before they feed on the party. |",
     "| **2** | **The Mirror Pool** | **Surreal:** The chamber is covered in still, black water that perfectly reflects the ceiling. Shadows move beneath the surface — until they don't. The \"reflection\" rises to attack. |",
     "| **3** | **The Living Silhouette** | **Suspense / Social:** A contact the party was supposed to meet is present — but wrong. They stand too still, speak too slowly. Their shadow moves independently. They don't know. |",
     "| **4** | **The Chain Reaction** | **Tactical Emergency:** The party arrived too late. Two bodies on the floor are already generating new shadows. The party has four rounds to destroy the original shadow before the room contains four of them. |",
     "| **5** | **The Sunlight Gambit** | **Puzzle Combat:** The only weapon effective enough is a *sunrod* or equivalent. The party has one. They must share it, pass it, and never let the shadows knock it from their hands. |",
     "| **6** | **The Shadow Museum** | **Atmospheric:** The room contains dozens of perfectly preserved humanoid silhouettes frozen on the walls — former victims whose shadows were peeled off and pinned. Their expressions are visible in the dark. |",
     "| **7** | **The Tracker** | **Mounting Dread:** A shadow has been following the party through the dungeon for two rooms. It hasn't attacked. It's learned their patrol patterns. It's waiting for the party to separate. |",
     "| **8** | **The Blind Friar** | **Character Moment:** A blind monk is sitting calmly in the center of a shadow-infested room, completely unharmed. He explains shadows are drawn to *sight* — they cannot see him and have no interest in the blind. He offers passage if the party extinguishes every light source and navigates by sound alone. |",
     "| **9** | **The Sunken Cathedral** | **Grim Gothic:** An entire chapel has been taken by shadows. Candlelight flickers; pews are overturned. The shadows treat this as their domain and are protective of it in a way that almost suggests reverence. |",
     "| **10** | **The Greater Shadow's Bargain** | **Dark Negotiation:** A greater shadow can communicate through writing — it forms letters in the frost on the walls. It offers to lead the party safely through the dungeon in exchange for one shadow freely given. It will abide by the deal. Whether to trust it is another matter. |"
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Darkened Scene (Investigation & Clues)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Discovery | Investigative Hook |",
     "|:----|:----------|:------------------|",
     "| **1** | **The Shadowless Corpse** | A body on the floor casts no shadow in any light. The shadow was torn free before the creature died. Something pulled it deliberately. |",
     "| **2** | **The Cold Brand** | The stone floor in the center of the room is several degrees colder than the rest. A DC 13 Arcana check identifies this as the resting spot of a shadow that has been here for decades. |",
     "| **3** | **The Weakened Survivor** | A prisoner in the room is alive but barely — their Strength is at 1, their eyes are sunken, their skin is waxen. The shadow fed on them repeatedly without killing them. It was keeping them. |",
     "| **4** | **The Midnight Graffiti** | Words are scratched into the wall at ground level, written in a shaky hand: *\"DO NOT LET IT DARK.\"* Below that, more words, much weaker: *\"IT CAME WHEN THE TORCH WENT OUT.\"* |",
     "| **5** | **The Fading Animals** | The dungeon's rat population has been killed — not eaten, not scattered, just drained. Tiny shadowless bodies litter the corners, skin and bone, as if their life-force was consumed. |",
     "| **6** | **The Shadow Map** | The shadows on the walls don't match the objects casting them. They're oriented differently, pointing toward a specific door or feature. A DC 14 Arcana check suggests the shadows are being magnetically drawn to something powerful and necrotic behind that door. |",
     "| **7** | **The Peeling Portrait** | A portrait on the wall depicts a noble in fine clothes. The shadow in the painting is subtly *wrong* — it moves independently. A DC 15 Arcana check reveals this is a shadow bound inside the painting by a binding ritual. Breaking it would release the shadow. |",
     "| **8** | **The Drained Shrine** | A shrine to a sun deity stands in the corner, its candles all burned to nothing, the holy symbol tarnished black. The shadows systematically destroyed every light source in the room before claiming it. |",
     "| **9** | **The Cracked Mirror** | A large mirror is shattered, its pieces scattered. Each shard reflects a slightly different angle — in one shard, a shadow is visible behind the viewer. In another, it isn't. One shard is missing entirely. |",
     "| **10** | **The Cultist's Confession** | A journal is found: a cultist deliberately attracted shadows to this location by performing an extended ritual in darkness. They believed the shadows were protective. The final entry is unfinished — the quill trailed off mid-sentence into a long, fading scratch. |"
    ]
   }
  ],
