  "src": "Wyvern.md",
  "customTables": [
   {
    "heading": "d10 Wyvern Encounters (Tone Variance Table)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Encounter Premise | Campaign Tone / Mechanics |",
     "|:----|:------------------|:--------------------------|",
     "| **1** | **The Dive Attack** | **Surprise Hit:** The wyvern drops from altitude in its first turn, making a full Multiattack with Bite, Sting, and Talons on the party's heaviest-armored member. Then it ascends and circles. |",
     "| **2** | **The Carried Away** | **Rescue Mission:** The wyvern grabbed a party member or NPC with its Talons and ascended. It's now circling at 60 ft. altitude. The grappled creature takes falling damage if released. Ranged attacks risk hitting the grappled person. |",
     "| **3** | **The Mounted Assault** | **Dual Threat:** A hobgoblin warlord is directing the wyvern from the saddle. Killing the rider causes the wyvern to fly to altitude and circle unpredictably. Targeting the wyvern first causes the rider to call in reinforcements. Both threats demand simultaneous attention. |",
     "| **4** | **The Lair Defense** | **Territory Encounter:** The party has stumbled into the wyvern's nesting territory. The wyvern isn't attacking for food — it's defending the nest. Its behavior is more frantic and reckless than a normal encounter; it will not retreat as long as the nest is threatened. |",
     "| **5** | **The Poison Crisis** | **HP Management:** A PC failed the Sting saving throw and took full poison damage. They're not dead, but they're at critical HP with a poisoned condition. The wyvern is still circling. The party has to finish the fight while managing a downed companion. |",
     "| **6** | **The Merchant Target** | **Mission Complication:** The party is escorting a merchant convoy. The wyvern attacks the horses and the wagon, not the adventurers. The adventurers have to protect the convoy while fighting something that can fly away and return. |",
     "| **7** | **The Canyon Fight** | **Vertical Terrain:** The encounter takes place in a ravine. The wyvern has superior maneuverability in the vertical dimension; ranged attackers can't get line of sight to the top of its arc. The party must lure it to ground level to fight effectively. |",
     "| **8** | **The Trained Guard** | **Dungeon Encounter:** A dungeon faction has a wyvern chained in an exterior courtyard or large chamber as a guardian. The chain is 60 ft. long. The wyvern has a keeper who feeds it but can't actually control it during combat. |",
     "| **9** | **The Starving Predator** | **Territorial Desperation:** The wyvern is thin — its normal hunting range has been depleted by another predator moving in. It is taking greater risks than a healthy wyvern would, attacking in poor conditions and refusing to retreat. It's more dangerous and more pitiable. |",
     "| **10** | **The Wyvern King** | **Regional Threat:** This wyvern is enormous — an ancient specimen that has lived in this area for fifty years. Local folklore mentions it. Hunters have a bounty on it. The warlord who rides it (if applicable) has named it and treats it as a partner. Its HP is 150. Its Sting DC is 17. |"
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Wyvern's Domain (Investigation & Clues)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Discovery | Investigative Hook |",
     "|:----|:----------|:------------------|",
     "| **1** | **The Poison Victim** | A body with a single small puncture wound and no other trauma. The victim's expression is frozen in surprise. A DC 11 Medicine check identifies wyvern poison as the cause of death. |",
     "| **2** | **The Stripped Carcass** | A large animal carcass — a horse, a bear, an elk — with its chest torn open and large talon gouges in the hide. The wyvern ate its fill in place. The tracks show it landed to feed, not just struck from above. |",
     "| **3** | **The Territorial Boundary** | Bleached bones arranged at irregular intervals along a trail — the wyvern's cached kills marking its territory edge. A DC 13 Nature check reads this as intentional territorial marking, not coincidence. |",
     "| **4** | **The Nest Site** | High up (cliff face, ruined tower, large cave mouth), a mess of large sticks, animal hide, and bones. The nest is large enough to hold a horse. It may contain eggs. It may be currently occupied. |",
     "| **5** | **The Shadow Report** | Local NPC or journal entry describes a recurring \"darkness across the sun, like a very large bird\" in the early morning. The sightings all come from the same direction, suggesting the wyvern's hunting route passes overhead at dawn. |",
     "| **6** | **The Saddle Rig** | A wyvern-sized leather harness, custom made, with stirrups sized for a Medium humanoid, is found mounted on the wall of a dungeon garrison. Someone has been flying this wyvern. The harness bears the sigil of a specific warband or noble house. |",
     "| **7** | **The Livestock Losses** | A farming community has lost seven animals in two weeks — taken from open fields, not from pens. The wounds (talon pattern, no blood trail) confirm aerial predation. The locals want it stopped; they're offering a reward. |",
     "| **8** | **The Poisoned Ground** | The soil around a wyvern nest is lightly toxic — the musk secreted for territorial marking accumulates over years. A DC 13 Nature check identifies the cause. The vegetation is dead in a 20-foot radius of the nest entrance. |",
     "| **9** | **The Failed Taming** | A dungeon journal describes an attempt to train a wyvern using a magical bridle. The entries grow shorter and more desperate over two weeks. The final entry is just a date and the words \"It is free.\" The bridle is in this room. The wyvern is somewhere in this dungeon. |",
     "| **10** | **The Warlord's Correspondence** | A sealed letter in a goblinoid warlord's writing describes the wyvern: its name, its hunting patterns, its weaknesses (a scar on its left flank where a prior attacker landed a telling blow), and where to find the keeper who controls it. The letter was addressed to an ally who never received it. |"
    ]
   }
  ],
