  "customTables": [
   {
    "heading": "d10 Zombie Encounters (Tone Variance Table)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Encounter Premise | Campaign Tone / Mechanics |",
     "|:----|:------------------|:--------------------------|",
     "| **1** | **The Herd** | **Survival Horror:** A dozen zombies are slowly converging on a barricaded door the party is behind. They aren't fast, but the barricade will give out in three rounds. |",
     "| **2** | **The Town Watch** | **Tragic:** The zombie patrol is still wearing the tabards of the local militia. A DC 12 History check lets a PC recognize a name on a breastplate. Someone the party met in a previous session. |",
     "| **3** | **The Bait** | **Tactical:** A necromancer is using a cluster of zombies as a distraction — obvious, noisy, shambling — while animated skeletons or a different threat flanks the party from the shadows. |",
     "| **4** | **The Resurrection Gone Wrong** | **Darkly Humorous:** An apprentice necromancer was attempting to raise their beloved mentor as an intelligent undead. It didn't go well. The mentor is now a zombie who keeps almost saying their apprentice's name but can't quite get the word out. The apprentice is devastated and hostile. |",
     "| **5** | **The Cattle Drive** | **Epic Scale:** The PCs crest a hill to find a necromancer herding fifty zombies toward a frontier town. The herd is slow. There may be time to warn the town, find a chokepoint, or kill the herder before the wave arrives. |",
     "| **6** | **The Fortified Shambler** | **Action Puzzle:** Someone has strapped crude armor and a spike-covered shield to an ogre zombie. It's barely functional, but the metal plating raises its AC to 14. The party must figure out how to target its weak points. |",
     "| **7** | **The Infected Survivor** | **Moral Dilemma:** A survivor the party has been escorting is showing symptoms of Zombie Rot. They haven't turned. There may be time to find a cure. Or there may not. The survivor knows it. |",
     "| **8** | **The Waking Market** | **Surreal / Unsettling:** The party enters what looks like a frozen, silent village market. Every stall is tended by a zombie in merchant's clothing, each one performing the motions of commerce but selling nothing, making no sound, serving no one. |",
     "| **9** | **The Flood** | **Environmental Hazard:** A channel of water separates the party from their goal. The water is full of zombies — too many to count — walking along the bottom. They cannot drown. They simply walk. |",
     "| **10** | **The Ogre's Tantrum** | **High Action:** An ogre zombie has partially broken free of its control and is now smashing through *both* the necromancer's defenses and the party's path of escape, indiscriminate and furious. |"
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "d10 The Rot Scene (Investigation & Clues)",
    "die": "d10",
    "rows": [
     "| d10 | Discovery | Investigative Hook |",
     "|:----|:----------|:------------------|",
     "| **1** | **The Feeding Trough** | A long stone trough is filled with rotting offal. The zombies were being maintained — whoever ran this place was feeding the undead to slow their decomposition. |",
     "| **2** | **The Bite Mark** | A dead body found in the room has a distinctive bite pattern from a zombie. A DC 13 Medicine check identifies that the victim was bitten *after* they were already dead — the zombie was feeding on a corpse, not killing. Implies it was recently animated from something that died naturally. |",
     "| **3** | **The Branded Dead** | Every zombie in the area has the same brand on its left forearm — a merchant's mark or a cult symbol. These people were enslaved before they were killed. |",
     "| **4** | **The Child's Drawing** | A crude drawing is pinned to the wall — stick figures, a house, a sun. One of the zombies in the room is child-sized. Someone in this dungeon has done something unforgivable. |",
     "| **5** | **The Ledger** | A necromancer's log tracks the zombies by number, not name. The entries stop abruptly three weeks ago. The last entry reads \"containment failing.\" |",
     "| **6** | **The Survivor Account** | A barely-alive prisoner in the room whispers that the zombies were locals — kidnapped from nearby farms over the past month. They can name the necromancer responsible. |",
     "| **7** | **The Resistance** | One zombie behaves slightly differently — it hesitates, it twitches, it doesn't immediately attack. A DC 15 Arcana or Insight check suggests a sliver of will is still fighting the animation. *Lesser restoration* or a *dispel magic* at 3rd level might free it — revealing a witness. |",
     "| **8** | **The Rotter's Trail** | Drag marks and rotting flesh scraps lead from this room to a larger chamber beyond. Something *very large* was recently animated here and dragged out. |",
     "| **9** | **The Mass Grave** | A concealed floor panel opens onto a pit filled with bodies in various stages of decomposition — a supply depot of future zombies. Some of the bodies at the bottom are still fresh. |",
     "| **10** | **The Mirror** | A full-length mirror hangs in the zombie-infested room. Zombies don't react to reflections. The mirror is enchanted — a scrying focus. Someone has been watching through it. |"
    ]
   }
  ],
